Subject: [PATCH 06881/11362] [outer-loop] ARC r11l round-5: honest null, L6
 three-part-payload mechanic mapped

Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on r11l explores L6: the cargo mechanic
expands from complementary pairs (L5) to two three-part payloads (9+15+14
for the upper-right socket, 6+11+10 for the lower-left). Solid colors 8,
13, 12 are decoys, and the orange+magenta dotted socket is impossible (no
solid orange cargo exists). L5's selection-occlusion mechanic generalizes:
an exposed-looking handle's first destination can still silently reject
if it intersects the fused payload. Best run placed both payloads deep
into their sockets but hit the 60-action hard cutoff before winning.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
